---
import Layout from '/src/components/main.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import AntiFlock from '/src/media/anti-flock.png';
---

<Layout title="Community Defense Committee" description="The Community Defense Committee is Bloomington DSA's anti-I.C.E. and anti-police surveillence committee'." headline="is protecting workers from I.C.E. and police surveillence through the Community Defense Committee.">

<!-- 
hey, CDC!

everything between the two `<Layout>` tags is editable HTML.
you can change the page title, the SEO description, and most importantly, the headline that serves as the menu element 

if you want to add images, place them in the `/src/media/community-defense-committee/` folder. 
if you want to import a specific image, you have to give it a name. you can do that by adding a line like `import NameInTitleCase from '/src/media/community-defense-committee/YOURPHOTO.png';`. This creates an optimized version of the image you can add to the page using the special image tag: `<Image src={NameInTitleCase} alt="your alt text would go here."`

if you wanted to add many images as a gallery, check out the bash folder. 
 -->

<section>

<div style='margin: auto;display: flex;justify-content: center;align-items: center;height:60vh; width: 400px;max-width: calc(100vw - 4em);background-image: url("/grain.png"), url("/grain.png") background-size: 64px 64px;background-color:#ec1f27;border-radius: 1em;'>
  <Image src={AntiFlock} alt="Anti-Flock text" style="height: 70%;max-width: 70%;object-fit: scale-down;"/>
</div>

<br>

<p>Want to get involved? <a href="/calendar">Join an upcoming Committee or General meeting on our calendar</a>!</p>

</section>


</Layout>
